{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490038-mages-and-ghouldom","id":1490038,"title":"Mages and Ghouldom","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-13T10:19:21-07:00","id":1490038,"title":"Mages and Ghouldom","content":"I've got a question that's been plaguing me for some time.<br /> <br /> Mages, upon Awakening, lose access to any linear magic they had previously. Their magick is more &quot;natural&quot; to them, and all things are seen through the lens of the Avatar and their Paradigm. Fair enough, I can't argue with that, especially given linear magic doesn't have the one main drawback of dynamic magick and the game needs that balancing tool to remain important, so people aren't crossing the sub-splat and the main splat for power gaming.<br /> <br /> But... what about ghouls?<br /> <br /> Vampiric Disciplines are, if I recall from the book correctly, counted as a type of linear magic in Mage. At the very least, they're described as such. Would a ghouled Mage, then, be unable to use the Disciplines gained by becoming a ghoul? What, then, is the point of becoming a ghoul as a Mage? Pseudo-Immortality aside.<br /> <br /> What about Thaumaturgy, which functions more like a Discipline than a path of Sorcery? Could a Mage who has been ghouled learn Thaumaturgy and use it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27513-screeb7165","name":"Screeb7165","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27513_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T10:42:33-07:00","id":1490039,"title":"","content":"As far as I know, yes. The common wisdom is that no mage would bother; but it's not something that's off limits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T11:12:05-07:00","id":1490040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Screeb7165</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490038-mages-and-ghouldom#post1490038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got a question that's been plaguing me for some time.<br /> <br /> Mages, upon Awakening, lose access to any linear magic they had previously. Their magick is more &amp;quot;natural&amp;quot; to them, and all things are seen through the lens of the Avatar and their Paradigm. Fair enough, I can't argue with that, especially given linear magic doesn't have the one main drawback of dynamic magick and the game needs that balancing tool to remain important, so people aren't crossing the sub-splat and the main splat for power gaming.<br /> <br /> But... what about ghouls?<br /> <br /> Vampiric Disciplines are, if I recall from the book correctly, counted as a type of linear magic in Mage. At the very least, they're described as such. Would a ghouled Mage, then, be unable to use the Disciplines gained by becoming a ghoul? What, then, is the point of becoming a ghoul as a Mage? Pseudo-Immortality aside.<br /> <br /> What about Thaumaturgy, which functions more like a Discipline than a path of Sorcery? Could a Mage who has been ghouled learn Thaumaturgy and use it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think ghoul Mages should be allowed to use the Disciplines they would normally gain for being ghouls. Disciplines are not linear Magic, they\u2019re something else entirely. Plus it would make it kinda pointless to become a ghoul if you couldn\u2019t even use Disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T11:45:49-07:00","id":1490043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490038-mages-and-ghouldom?p=1490039#post1490039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I know, yes. The common wisdom is that no mage would bother; but it's not something that's off limits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then why on Earth is &quot;Ghoul&quot; a Merit in M20? If you don't get Disciplines, what's even the point? The drawbacks are huge, especially if you use the optional rules that reduce your Magickal ability over time (which I think are stupid, personally).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490038-mages-and-ghouldom?p=1490040#post1490040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think ghoul Mages should be allowed to use the Disciplines they would normally gain for being ghouls. Disciplines are not linear Magic, they\u2019re something else entirely. Plus it would make it kinda pointless to become a ghoul if you couldn\u2019t even use Disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's also broadly my opinion, though I was curious what the metaphysics of Mage had to say about how that interacts. What about Thaumaturgy or other blood &quot;sorcery?&quot; What's your take on ghoul Mages using those?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27513-screeb7165","name":"Screeb7165","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27513_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T11:58:10-07:00","id":1490044,"title":"","content":"I think ghoul mages should be allowed to use blood sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T13:37:22-07:00","id":1490055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Screeb7165</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490038-mages-and-ghouldom?p=1490043#post1490043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then why on Earth is &quot;Ghoul&quot; a Merit in M20? If you don't get Disciplines, what's even the point? The drawbacks are huge, especially if you use the optional rules that reduce your Magickal ability over time (which I think are stupid, personally).</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said that you don't get Disciplines. I also never said that you don't get blood magic (though by a strict reading of the Merit, you could only get it if ghouled by someone from a Clan that has blood magic). I said that mages wouldn't bother; Spheres are vastly superior.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T13:58:04-07:00","id":1490058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Screeb7165</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490038-mages-and-ghouldom?p=1490043#post1490043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then why on Earth is &quot;Ghoul&quot; a Merit in M20? If you don't get Disciplines, what's even the point? The drawbacks are huge, especially if you use the optional rules that reduce your Magickal ability over time (which I think are stupid, personally).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the confusion here comes from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> answering multiple different questions with a single 'yes'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Screeb7165</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490038-mages-and-ghouldom#post1490038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a ghouled Mage, then, be unable to use the Disciplines gained by becoming a ghoul?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. A ghouled Mage would be able to learn Disciplines up to the limit set by the Generation of the Donor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Screeb7165</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490038-mages-and-ghouldom#post1490038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What, then, is the point of becoming a ghoul as a Mage? Pseudo-Immortality aside.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. A cheat-code for access to Linear Magic (see below)<br /> 2. Access to vitae. That stuff is basically dirty Tass, with an additional heap of powerful magick properties. Problem is, it's probably in the Mage's body.<br /> 3. Limited Bloodpool as additional power reservoir<br /> 4. Healing<br /> Generally not the greatest benefits in exchange for thralldom and addiction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Screeb7165</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490038-mages-and-ghouldom#post1490038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about Thaumaturgy, which functions more like a Discipline than a path of Sorcery? Could a Mage who has been ghouled learn Thaumaturgy and use it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Unfortunately, it is still limited by the potency of the Donor vitae as any other Discipline. Although it is technically Linear Magic, it is Blood Magic. The 'power source' is vitae, and thus different from Faith, Will, or Formulae that fuel other Numina.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 08-13-2022, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T14:02:15-07:00","id":1490060,"title":"","content":"I answered the final question that was asked with a \u201cyes.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T14:08:24-07:00","id":1490061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490038-mages-and-ghouldom?p=1490055#post1490055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never said that you don't get Disciplines. I also never said that you don't get blood magic (though by a strict reading of the Merit, you could only get it if ghouled by someone from a Clan that has blood magic). I said that mages wouldn't bother; Spheres are vastly superior.</div> </div> </div> </div>Woops. My bad! I misunderstood. Indeed, Spheres are vastly superior, and it is a rare Mage indeed who would actually see use in Ghouldom.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490038-mages-and-ghouldom?p=1490058#post1490058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Truncated]</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to see I was on the right track, then. I'm the Mage expert in my VTM group, and workshopped with our ST a (very, very small) faction of Mages ghouled by a renegade Tremere, and it only struck me in the last few days that <i>maybe</i> blood sorcery might fall under the umbrella of that <i>sorcery stuff</i> Mages can't do anymore.<br /> (Yes, I know, out of context that faction sounds ridiculous, but we're having fun and that's what matters &lt;3)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27513-screeb7165","name":"Screeb7165","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27513_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T14:25:15-07:00","id":1490064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Screeb7165</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490038-mages-and-ghouldom?p=1490061#post1490061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Woops. My bad! I misunderstood. Indeed, Spheres are vastly superior, and it is a rare Mage indeed who would actually see use in Ghouldom.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Glad to see I was on the right track, then. I'm the Mage expert in my VTM group, and workshopped with our ST a (very, very small) faction of Mages ghouled by a renegade Tremere, and it only struck me in the last few days that <i>maybe</i> blood sorcery might fall under the umbrella of that <i>sorcery stuff</i> Mages can't do anymore.<br /> (Yes, I know, out of context that faction sounds ridiculous, but we're having fun and that's what matters &lt;3)</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad you guys are having fun \ud83d\ude0a","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T14:33:10-07:00","id":1490065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Screeb7165</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490038-mages-and-ghouldom?p=1490061#post1490061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Yes, I know, out of context that faction sounds ridiculous, but we're having fun and that's what matters &lt;3)</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't really sound absurd, even if the Tremere wasn't a renegade. Both factions can gain from it, in fact. The Tremere have struggled with their loss of Dynamic Magic for centuries (even though they would never admit to that openly) and the recent Sorcerer supplement for M20 contains a short box pointing out how Mages can develop new Paths, even though they are unable to use them. Having ghouled Mages makes perfect sense if the goal is to research new Paths and push the limits of Blood Sorcery.<br /> For the Mages, the negative impact of ghouldom <i>sucks</i>, but if they play nice, they gain the power of Clan Tremere as allies on a logistical and political level. The Tremere have immense resources and influence. The potential access to arcane knowledge alone is probably tempting enough for a Mage, add to that the ability of the Clan to 'pull some strings' within Sleeper society.<br /> The point is, aside from the mechanical pros/cons of the Ghoul Merit, it's easy to forget that there is also a potential social and resource power gain. It's playing with fire for sure, but for some the risk may be worth it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 08-13-2022, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T15:23:39-07:00","id":1490071,"title":"","content":"I don't think that the box in S20 would translate to Blood Sorcery: they're specifically about creating Paths for mortal sorcerers (where the power source is \u201cformulae\u201d, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a> put it, not \u201cvitae\u201d \u2014 and also not Faith or Will, for that matter: <i>just</i> Hedge Magic; not Psychic Phenomena, True Faith, or Blood Sorcery). I also question the notion that the Tremere have any arcane secrets that mages would be interested in \u2014 again, largely because of the conceptual differences between Blood Sorcery and Awakened Magick. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, V20 Black Hand has the \u201cdirty secret\u201d of Blood Familiars (pp.152\u2013154) which allows vampires to \u201cborrow\u201d a mage's Magick (or mages to \u201cloan\u201d their Magick to vampires). If a Tremere were ever to learn of this secret, that could easily motivate him to try to reconcile with the Order of Hermes or other Awakened Mages to try to \u201cget back\u201d what Tremere lost. V20 Black Hand frames this in terms of Archaic Sorcery (i.e., a hitherto unknown Dark Ages: Mage Fellowship that has survived into the present while still practicing DA:Mage-style Foundation and Pillars magic); but it could easily be adapted for \u201cmodern mages\u201d with very little trouble. In fact, the only adjustment that would need to be made, in my opinion, would be to the \u201cOffering the Awakened Soul\u201d Rote: it's listed as \u201cDeva \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u201d which makes sense in the context of Itarajana Sorcery (pp.147\u2013151) but not when the mage in question uses Arete and Spheres. The Deva Pillar is effectively a blend of Prime and Mind; so I'd make this a Prime/Mind Rote, requiring five dots in at least one of those Spheres, maybe both. <br /> <br /> You're right about the \u201cmundane\u201d benefits of being a ghoul, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-14-2022, 10:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T05:48:50-07:00","id":1490123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490038-mages-and-ghouldom?p=1490071#post1490071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that the box in S20 would translate to Blood Sorcery: they're specifically about creating Paths for mortal sorcerers (where the power source is \u201cformulae\u201d, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a> put it, not \u201cvitae\u201d \u2014 and also not Faith or Will, for that matter: <i>just</i> Hedge Magic; not Psychic Phenomena, True Faith, or Blood Sorcery). I also question the notion that the Tremere have any arcane secrets that mages would be interested in \u2014 again, largely because of the conceptual differences between Blood Sorcery and Awakened Magick.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, V20 Black Hand has the \u201cdirty secret\u201d of Blood Familiars (pp.152\u2013154) which allows vampires to \u201cborrow\u201d a mage's Magick (or mages to \u201cloan\u201d their Magick to vampires). If a Tremere were ever to learn of this secret, that could easily motivate him to try to reconcile with the Order of Hermes or other Awakened Mages to try to \u201cget back\u201d what Tremere lost. V20 Black Hand frames this in terms of Archaic Sorcery (i.e., a hitherto unknown Dark Ages: Mage Fellowship that has survived into the present whole still practicing DA:Mage-style \u201cArchaic Sorcery\u201d); but it could easily be adapted for \u201cmodern mages\u201d with very little trouble. In fact, the only adjustment that would need to be made, in my opinion, would be to the \u201cOffering the Awakened Soul\u201d Rote: it's listed as \u201cDeva \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u201d which makes sense in the context of Itarajana Sorcery (pp.147\u2013151) but not when the mage in question uses Arete and Spheres. The Deva Pillar is effectively a blend of Prime and Mind; so I'd make this a Prime/Mind Rote, requiring five dots in at least one of those Spheres, maybe both.<br /> <br /> You're right about the \u201cmundane\u201d benefits of being a ghoul, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The second massasa war happened because you had young hermetic mages raiding a Tremere chantry looking for secrets. I think the oldest members of the clan do have secrets that would be interesting to know. But outside of true names and alchemical recipes, most of the knowledge would nonsensical to modern mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","user":"Starcomet","date":". 08-14-2022, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T06:38:13-07:00","id":1490128,"title":"","content":"I never bought into the premise of <b>Blood Treachery</b>, for precisely this reason. Ironically, the infamous mage arrogance would have worked to prevent the Second Massasa War, because even if there <i>were</i> some secrets known by the Tremere that might have been interesting for mages to know, I doubt very much that there would have been any Hermetics willing to acknowledge that. \u201cWe have a banquet of arcane knowledge at our disposal; they have a few table scraps. Let's raid them for their table scraps!\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T06:53:44-07:00","id":1490129,"title":"","content":"I think it was mentioned that the raid occured because the Avatar storm swept by and all of the traditions had lost most/all of their archmages and thus a lot of lore and knowledge. They were just desparate to find something to make up for the lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T09:08:18-07:00","id":1490135,"title":"","content":"I don't buy it either,<i> in the way it was presented</i>: Some formulae stopped working cuz' &quot;reality&quot;, and some mages just &quot;decided&quot; that getting the <i>older </i>formulae was going to work better. Because it's not like we've spent the rest of Mage history declaring that things work the other way arround. Hermetics are dense, but I think that's close to caricaturesque.<br /> <br /> That being said, Tremere having some books from the &quot;golden age&quot; of the OoH, that may be of some value as bargaining chips, <i>does </i>make sense. I wouldn't have used that plot hook to justify the movilization of ALL echelons of the Order, but I do think a raid could be justified<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that the box in S20 would translate to Blood Sorcery: they're specifically about creating Paths for mortal sorcerers (where the power source is \u201cformulae\u201d, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a> put it, not \u201cvitae\u201d \u2014 and also not Faith or Will, for that matter: <i>just</i> Hedge Magic; not Psychic Phenomena, True Faith, or Blood Sorcery). I also question the notion that the Tremere have any arcane secrets that mages would be interested in \u2014 again, largely because of the conceptual differences between Blood Sorcery and Awakened Magick.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but maybe there could be a way to be discovered.<br /> <br /> Every mage of note that has been vampirized in the Lore developped Blood Magick. So it stands to reason that there's some relationship between the two that fascilitates the latter when you knew the former. A Ghoul Mage, having access to both, could have some helpful insigth to develop that type of magic.<br /> <br /> Tremere can do that already, but I think it makes some level of sense","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-14-2022, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T09:30:49-07:00","id":1490138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490038-mages-and-ghouldom?p=1490135#post1490135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every mage of note that has been vampirized in the Lore developped Blood Magick. So it stands to reason that there's some relationship between the two that fascilitates the latter when you knew the former. A Ghoul Mage, having access to both, could have some helpful insigth to develop that type of magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a rule in the Guide to the True Black Hand that an Embraced Mage gets to put half of the exp they spent on [Arete]* and their [Spheres]** towards Blood Magic, so I think it's more than simply &quot;standing to reason,&quot; it's actually baked into the text of the setting.<br /> <br /> *Foundation, in the book, due to being a form of Dark Ages style magick rather than modern<br /> **Pillars, for the same reason","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27513-screeb7165","name":"Screeb7165","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27513_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T09:54:55-07:00","id":1490141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490038-mages-and-ghouldom?p=1490135#post1490135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but maybe there could be a way to be discovered.<br /> <br /> Every mage of note that has been vampirized in the Lore developped Blood Magick. So it stands to reason that there's some relationship between the two that fascilitates the latter when you knew the former. A Ghoul Mage, having access to both, could have some helpful insigth to develop that type of magic.<br /> <br /> Tremere can do that already, but I think it makes some level of sense</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, upon re-reading my post it really looks like I was implying that the process in that box of S20 could be used to create new Blood Sorcery Paths. What I meant to say is that having ghouled Mages with actual access to basic Blood Magic is a good basis for researching a similar process for the same reasons you mentioned. Sorry, English is not my native language.<br /> <br /> It's interesting that the Nagaraja did not develop their own brand of Blood Magic. If I recall correctly, Nihilistics wasn't categorized as such (before it was folded into Necromancy and then Oblivion).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T10:25:27-07:00","id":1490146,"title":"","content":"And in a Vampire/Mage crossover game (where Kindred and Awakened are working side by side), I'd be inclined to be a bit more generous on such matters \u2014 just as I'd be inclined to go with the \u201cBlood Familiars\u201d concept in such a game, even if I were to reject the notion in every other context. <br /> <br /> So despite my earlier post, maybe it wouldn't be such a bad idea to allow that \u201cmages creating Paths\u201d rule from S20 to apply to Blood Magic as well \u2014 under the right circumstances. And perhaps the Blood Familiar concept could be the key to facilitating it. As written, establishing a Blood Familiar relationship between a vampire and a mage benefits the vampire (by letting it use Awakened Magick) but not the mage; for a game where the two are working in tandem, rather than the mages being treated as subservient, it would be appropriate to say that the mage gains access to whatever Blood Magic her vampiric partner has? And perhaps the mage could devise new Paths for her partner with her partner's assistance. <br /> <br /> All of this is non-canon, of course. But it's not <i>too</i> much of a stretch, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T13:01:09-07:00","id":1490165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490038-mages-and-ghouldom?p=1490146#post1490146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And in a Vampire/Mage crossover game (where Kindred and Awakened are working side by side), I'd be inclined to be a bit more generous on such matters \u2014 just as I'd be inclined to go with the \u201cBlood Familiars\u201d concept in such a game, even if I were to reject the notion in every other context. <br /> <br /> So despite my earlier post, maybe it wouldn't be such a bad idea to allow that \u201cmages creating Paths\u201d rule from S20 to apply to Blood Magic as well \u2014 under the right circumstances. And perhaps the Blood Familiar concept could be the key to facilitating it. As written, establishing a Blood Familiar relationship between a vampire and a mage benefits the vampire (by letting it use Awakened Magick) but not the mage; for a game where the two are working in tandem, rather than the mages being treated as subservient, it would be appropriate to say that the mage gains access to whatever Blood Magic her vampiric partner has? And perhaps the mage could devise new Paths for her partner with her partner's assistance. <br /> <br /> All of this is non-canon, of course. But it's not <i>too</i> much of a stretch, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Within limitations certainly. My first question is &quot;who pays the cost of the blood magic?&quot; If it's the Vampire, that actually gives the Mage an insane amount of power over the Vampire (because they can waste the Vamp's life force faster than the Vamp can accrue it, remotely, so if things get hostile, the Mage has a Paradox-free ranged &quot;you frenzy now&quot; button). If it's the Mage, that seriously limits its usefulness to the Mage, as they can only hold so much Vitae in their body.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the Mage pays Vitae or Quint to achieve a Blood Magic spell? The same way the Vamp can pay Vitae as though it were Quint when using True Magick?<br /> <br /> Either way, this would require an insane amount of trust on both parties' parts and would be a fascinating element in a campaign, and I am here for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27513-screeb7165","name":"Screeb7165","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27513_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T13:21:13-07:00","id":1490171,"title":"","content":"I was thinking that the mage would spend Q to fuel the borrowed Blood Magic. <br /> <br /> And yes, it would require an insane amount of trust. That's part of the point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T13:27:45-07:00","id":1490173,"title":"","content":"I want to say the Vampire is getting the better end of the deal, since Vitae is easier to come by than Quint, but giving a Mage an option to pull off even limited effects without Paradox is definitely spicy. Movement of the Mind, Path of Conjuration, Elemental Mastery, and Lure of Flames come to mind as ideal picks for a Hermetic dabbling in Thaumaturgy. Path of Mercury too, access depending. (My group in particular soft-banned that path due to how insanely good it is, given the only other teleport effects go to a single place, a specific person, are Elder powers, or are Koldunic Sorcery and not technically a teleport)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27513-screeb7165","name":"Screeb7165","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27513_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T13:28:19-07:00","id":1490174,"title":"","content":"Regardless I am furiously taking notes to integrate this into a Mage game I intend to run","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27513-screeb7165","name":"Screeb7165","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27513_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T13:40:41-07:00","id":1490178,"title":"","content":"I'm wary of \u201cX gets the better end of the deal\u201d arguments: if both parties get something that makes it worth it to them, and don't have to pay a price that they're unwilling to pay, then it's a reasonable deal. My problem with the Blood Familiars system as written is that it doesn't offer <i>any</i> benefits to the mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T13:43:46-07:00","id":1490179,"title":"","content":"Oh, full agreement. Apologies, my ADHD got the better of me. I suppose my point was &quot;if there was a negotiation about this, the Mage is likely to be more wary, because the Vampire is potentially getting more of the deal.&quot;<br /> <br /> Not necessarily a problem, just an observation.<br /> <br /> The Blood Familiars system definitely worked for what it was trying to do, though I agree that it really bites that as it exists in V20 it gives the Mage zilch. I enjoy the idea that it's a two way street, for better or worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27513-screeb7165","name":"Screeb7165","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27513_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T23:35:27-07:00","id":1490222,"title":"","content":"The advantage with Disciplines for a Mage is that they're static effects, and as such aren't affected by Paradox. They're also more likely to be rolled with a better pool or in other ways be easier to use than similar Magic, specially as they don't conflict with it. Even that single starting dot of Potence is a neat advantage as a static effect. You can also learn specific Disciplines as a means to access effects that would need a Sphere combination you don't have nor plan on getting anytime soon.<br /> <br /> Just don't use XP costs for Ghouls, use the costs for Vampires. The increased XP cost is the worse rule Ghouls have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T06:51:59-07:00","id":1490254,"title":"","content":"God, I forgot how damn expensive ghoul discipline costs are. Was it any better in Ghouls and Revenants?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27513-screeb7165","name":"Screeb7165","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27513_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T10:03:54-07:00","id":1490268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Screeb7165</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490038-mages-and-ghouldom?p=1490254#post1490254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">God, I forgot how damn expensive ghoul discipline costs are. Was it any better in Ghouls and Revenants?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately.<br /> <br /> I just personally ignore them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T11:17:34-07:00","id":1490274,"title":"","content":"Terrible. Out of clan costs it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27513-screeb7165","name":"Screeb7165","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27513_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T13:41:57-07:00","id":1490283,"title":"","content":"The key problem with being a Ghouled Mage is that it slowly but surely takes out your Avatar. Or at least puts it to sleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T14:02:24-07:00","id":1490287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490038-mages-and-ghouldom?p=1490283#post1490283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The key problem with being a Ghouled Mage is that it slowly but surely takes out your Avatar. Or at least puts it to sleep.</div> </div> </div> </div>AFAIK this rule is optional.<br /> <br /> But even if it isn't, IIRC it just affects gaining Arete. While that's a heavy thing, most characters will at some point reach their peak as the cost in XP and in-character development becomes just too much.<br /> <br /> Never being able to raise Arete again isn't that big of a drawback from a game perspective. Terrible for the character, not so much for the player. And I see no need to change that (after all, it isn't really a huge advantage, it is barely an advantage at all).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T16:32:45-07:00","id":1490313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490038-mages-and-ghouldom?p=1490287#post1490287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">AFAIK this rule is optional.<br /> <br /> But even if it isn't, IIRC it just affects gaining Arete. While that's a heavy thing, most characters will at some point reach their peak as the cost in XP and in-character development becomes just too much.<br /> <br /> Never being able to raise Arete again isn't that big of a drawback from a game perspective. Terrible for the character, not so much for the player. And I see no need to change that (after all, it isn't really a huge advantage, it is barely an advantage at all).</div> </div> </div> </div>Over in the guide to the true black hand, it freezes your [Arete] rating while ghouled. Book of Secrets doesn't make mention of this, but instead offers the optional rule that for every year the Mage remains a ghoul, they lose a dot of Avatar, and if they have no Avatar dots, they lose a dot of Arete.<br /> <br /> I understand why that rule was offered. It's to keep characters from trying to cross-splat. I just think it's excessive. Why should being a ghoul invoke a pseudo-gilgul?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27513-screeb7165","name":"Screeb7165","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27513_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T21:21:36-07:00","id":1490350,"title":"","content":"It had a lot to do with common game-design misconceptions of the time. There was no true professional RPG design until the 2000's, and only then we started to have a more solid body of knowledge in the area to draw on.<br /> <br /> So, they both considered cross-splat a form of combo, and as such an inherently bad thing, and that the game should drive the point of something being conceptually bad by making it mechanically bad for the player. Combos also should be prevented by punishing the player.<br /> <br /> All in all, player punishment was a big design dogma of the time. Any player that wanted this option should do so for the &quot;right&quot; reasons, and accepting the punishment would be their way of showing that. In this case, both to avoid a combo and because you're playing a Mage that is accepting something that is intrinsically linked in the lore to decay, corruption and stasis.<br /> <br /> Now, I personally think that the Blood Bond is enough of a drawback by itself. Even if it is actually a perfectly healthy relationship with someone that has your best interest in mind, or even with another PC, the emotional pull of an artificial obsession coupled with addiction should be horrible enough for the character.<br /> <br /> For the player... nothing, really. It's not all that much of an advantage for Mages. You must certainly pay something for any free Discipline dots, the other benefits are so-so, and while having access to a new set of powers is always good, you must pay for them as usual, so no big deal.<br /> <br /> The biggest issue is for player and ST to sit and discuss their expectations with this or any other effect that causes a crossover in game, because they have to be roughly on the same page. This can be an awesome opportunity or a burden depending on how the ST want to use Vampires and VtM lore in their game, or deviate from it, and how they want (or not) to use the Vampire NPCs that come attached (I do think that making them just downtime background is fair enough if the ST don't want to deal with them, but has no problem with the Mage with this condition).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}